1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,271
It's nine p.

2
00:00:01,271 --> 00:00:01,400
m.

3
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,878
You're out for dinner.

4
00:00:02,878 --> 00:00:08,147
Three decisions are waiting on you: a refund, a vendor invoice, a calendar clash.

5
00:00:08,147 --> 00:00:10,975
Your team is stuck until you find a laptop.

6
00:00:12,275 --> 00:00:14,892
Greenlight is an approval terminal for Even G2.

7
00:00:14,892 --> 00:00:19,459
One request at a time, checked against your own rules, answered with one gesture.

8
00:00:20,759 --> 00:00:24,120
Requests arrive from Telegram, Gmail and Google Calendar.

9
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:31,195
Policy Guard reads the amount first, with plain code, then asks a model to judge it against rules you wrote in English.

10
00:00:31,195 --> 00:00:35,677
If the model is down, the card still appears, flagged, with a fallback tag.

11
00:00:35,677 --> 00:00:37,092
The AI only recommends.

12
00:00:37,092 --> 00:00:39,097
Only your gesture sends anything.

13
00:00:40,397 --> 00:00:41,639
Setup takes a minute.

14
00:00:41,639 --> 00:00:42,999
Connect your accounts.

15
00:00:42,999 --> 00:00:46,784
Write two or three rules, the way you would brief an assistant.

16
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:52,047
Then pair your glasses with a six-digit code that works once and expires in ten minutes.

17
00:00:55,847 --> 00:01:00,392
Rohan asks for a three-twenty-dollar AWS refund in Telegram.

18
00:01:00,392 --> 00:01:04,331
One card: what, who, and a one-line recommendation.

19
00:01:04,331 --> 00:01:05,542
Tap to approve.

20
00:01:05,542 --> 00:01:11,678
You get three seconds to undo, and then the reply lands right under his message.

21
00:01:12,978 --> 00:01:15,737
A nine-hundred-dollar invoice arrives by email.

22
00:01:15,737 --> 00:01:19,552
It breaks your five-hundred-dollar rule, so the card is flagged.

23
00:01:19,552 --> 00:01:23,427
Hold to decline, and a polite reply goes back on the same thread.

24
00:01:24,727 --> 00:01:27,162
A new invite overlaps your investor call.

25
00:01:27,162 --> 00:01:29,836
Flagged against your no-double-booking rule.

26
00:01:29,836 --> 00:01:32,093
Decline it, and the calendar updates.

27
00:01:33,393 --> 00:01:40,716
Every decision is logged: who asked, the verdict, what you chose, and whether the model or the fallback judged it.

28
00:01:40,716 --> 00:01:43,607
This is the real dashboard, running locally.

29
00:01:44,907 --> 00:01:45,817
Three promises.

30
00:01:45,817 --> 00:01:48,364
Nothing is sent until the countdown ends.

31
00:01:48,364 --> 00:01:50,305
A double tap never sends twice.

32
00:01:50,305 --> 00:01:52,367
And Greenlight never moves funds.

33
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:53,580
Demo accounts only.

34
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:01,657
Built during the hackathon: more than eighty commits, a hundred and eighty-eight tests, three channels, one glasses app.

35
00:02:01,657 --> 00:02:05,329
The code, the tests and the dashboard are all in the repository.

36
00:02:06,629 --> 00:02:07,256
Greenlight.

37
00:02:07,256 --> 00:02:08,281
Read the request.

38
00:02:08,281 --> 00:02:09,307
Trust your rules.

39
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:10,390
Decide in one tap.
